WEBVTT

00:00:02.452 --> 00:00:04.484
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:04.522 --> 00:00:05.378
Sammy!

00:00:06.117 --> 00:00:08.088
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:08.111 --> 00:00:08.674
Go!

00:00:12.393 --> 00:00:13.601
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:14.208 --> 00:00:15.686
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:19.521 --> 00:00:22.923
This is dad's book. I think dad
wants us to pick up where he left off.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.876
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:27.519
Family business. Do you think
Mom wanted all this for us?

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:28.645
I can't do this alone.

00:00:29.412 --> 00:00:30.163
I'm driving.

00:01:02.547 --> 00:01:04.416
Man, these are some phat houses, huh?

00:01:04.792 --> 00:01:05.923
I'd like to live here.

00:01:06.261 --> 00:01:06.599
Yeah.

00:01:07.162 --> 00:01:08.708
Too bad you can't afford it.

00:01:09.662 --> 00:01:10.837
Yeah, you're right.

00:01:11.512 --> 00:01:13.850
This neighborhood will be
damn expensive when it's done.

00:01:38.628 --> 00:01:39.899
This place is perfect...

00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:40.903
Ow!

00:01:42.097 --> 00:01:43.283
...Except for the mosquitoes.

00:01:47.349 --> 00:01:48.100
Aah!

00:01:49.264 --> 00:01:49.744
Dustin?

00:01:50.849 --> 00:01:52.183
Help me, I'm trapped!

00:01:53.135 --> 00:01:54.416
I broke my ankle.

00:01:55.969 --> 00:01:56.991
I'll get a rope!

00:01:59.659 --> 00:02:00.537
Oh, damn.

00:02:17.709 --> 00:02:18.664
Oh god!

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:30.749
Travis, help!

00:02:30.911 --> 00:02:31.710
Hang on!

00:02:42.035 --> 00:02:43.513
Travis, help!

00:02:43.973 --> 00:02:45.775
Aah! Aaah!

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:47.525
It's okay, Dustin. It's okay.

00:02:50.964 --> 00:02:51.517
Dustin?

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:53.907
Dustin, I'm here.

00:02:56.182 --> 00:02:56.945
Oh, god.

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:06.603
<i>I got something to say.</i>

00:03:23.221 --> 00:03:23.936
<i>Ow!</i>

00:03:26.452 --> 00:03:27.648
<i>Yeah, you're doing all right.</i>

00:03:27.664 --> 00:03:29.282
<i>Gonna start a fire</i>

00:03:32.558 --> 00:03:34.478
You know, we could get
day jobs once in a while.

00:03:35.342 --> 00:03:36.468
Hunting's our day job,

00:03:36.984 --> 00:03:38.110
And the pay is crap.

00:03:38.357 --> 00:03:39.518
Yeah, but hustling pool,

00:03:40.254 --> 00:03:41.158
Credit-Card scams?

00:03:41.842 --> 00:03:43.513
It's not the most honest
thing in the world, Dean.

00:03:43.743 --> 00:03:44.804
Well, let's see... Honest...

00:03:45.795 --> 00:03:46.506
Fun and easy...

00:03:47.964 --> 00:03:48.879
It's no contest.

00:03:49.075 --> 00:03:49.484
Besides,

00:03:50.055 --> 00:03:51.404
We're good at it. It's
what we were raised to do.

00:03:51.473 --> 00:03:54.284
How we were raised was
jacked. Yeah, says you.

00:03:54.717 --> 00:03:56.328
We got a new gig or what? Maybe.

00:03:56.568 --> 00:03:59.203
Oasis Plains, Oklahoma.
Not far from here.

00:03:59.498 --> 00:04:00.856
Gas-Company employee.

00:04:01.626 --> 00:04:03.362
Dustin Burwash,

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.907
Supposedly died from creutzfeldt-Jakob.

00:04:06.244 --> 00:04:06.584
Huh?

00:04:07.229 --> 00:04:09.399
Human mad cow disease. Mad cow?

00:04:10.525 --> 00:04:11.856
Wasn't that on "Oprah"?

00:04:12.402 --> 00:04:13.428
You watch "Oprah"?

00:04:16.713 --> 00:04:19.531
So this guy eats a bad burger.
Why is it our kind of thing?

00:04:20.748 --> 00:04:23.528
Mad cow disease causes
massive brain degeneration.

00:04:23.531 --> 00:04:25.998
It takes months, even years
for the damage to appear,

00:04:26.004 --> 00:04:27.188
But this guy, Dustin,

00:04:27.376 --> 00:04:29.994
Sounds like his brain
disintegrated in about an hour,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.258
Maybe less.

00:04:31.275 --> 00:04:32.748
Okay, that's weird. Yeah.

00:04:33.217 --> 00:04:34.523
Now, it could be a disease,

00:04:35.184 --> 00:04:36.710
Or it could be something much nastier.

00:04:37.658 --> 00:04:39.301
All right, Oklahoma.

00:04:39.947 --> 00:04:41.429
Man, work, work, work.

00:04:42.339 --> 00:04:43.733
No time to spend my money.

00:04:44.862 --> 00:04:48.770
<i>We got the power, we got the glory</i>

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:51.020
<i>Just say you need it...</i>

00:04:58.851 --> 00:04:59.802
Travis Weaver?

00:05:01.561 --> 00:05:02.358
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:03.715 --> 00:05:05.756
Are you the Travis who
worked with uncle Dusty?

00:05:06.776 --> 00:05:08.489
Dustin never mentioned nephews.

00:05:09.052 --> 00:05:09.650
Really?

00:05:10.108 --> 00:05:11.316
Well, he sure mentioned you.

00:05:11.363 --> 00:05:12.829
He said you were the greatest.

00:05:13.275 --> 00:05:14.037
Oh, he did?

00:05:14.525 --> 00:05:15.182
Huh.

00:05:15.898 --> 00:05:17.681
So, we wanted to ask you...

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.417
What exactly happened out there?

00:05:20.801 --> 00:05:21.693
I'm not sure.

00:05:22.168 --> 00:05:24.866
He fell in the sinkhole. I went
to the truck to get some rope, and

00:05:25.382 --> 00:05:26.696
By the time I got back...

00:05:27.412 --> 00:05:28.620
What'd you see?

00:05:30.145 --> 00:05:30.591
Nothing.

00:05:31.313 --> 00:05:32.052
Just Dustin.

00:05:32.134 --> 00:05:33.870
No wounds or anything?

00:05:34.316 --> 00:05:35.231
Well, he was bleeding

00:05:35.442 --> 00:05:37.846
From his eyes and his ears, his nose,

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:39.242
That's it.

00:05:39.876 --> 00:05:41.670
So do you think it could
be this whole mad cow thing?

00:05:43.366 --> 00:05:44.035
I don't know.

00:05:44.645 --> 00:05:45.853
That's what the doctors are saying.

00:05:45.923 --> 00:05:46.827
But if it was,

00:05:47.472 --> 00:05:51.824
He would have acted strange beforehand,
like dementia, loss of motor control.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.821
You ever notice anything like that? No.

00:05:54.199 --> 00:05:54.752
No way.

00:05:56.002 --> 00:05:58.316
Yeah, but if it wasn't some
disease, what the hell was it?

00:05:59.517 --> 00:06:00.395
That's a good question.

00:06:00.599 --> 00:06:00.972
Yep.

00:06:01.182 --> 00:06:02.595
Can you tell us where this happened?

00:06:03.361 --> 00:06:03.751
Yeah.

00:06:27.568 --> 00:06:28.024
Huh.

00:06:29.575 --> 00:06:30.296
What do you think?

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.002
I don't know,

00:06:32.017 --> 00:06:34.607
But if that guy Travis was right,
it happened pretty damn fast.

00:06:35.389 --> 00:06:36.200
So what?

00:06:36.523 --> 00:06:38.175
Some sort of creature
chewed on his brain?

00:06:38.198 --> 00:06:39.625
No, there'd be an entry wound.

00:06:40.046 --> 00:06:41.744
Sounds like this thing
worked from the inside.

00:06:45.579 --> 00:06:46.105
Huh.

00:06:47.232 --> 00:06:49.088
It looks like there's only room for one.

00:06:49.899 --> 00:06:50.966
You want to flip a coin?

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.240
Dean, we have no idea what's down there.

00:06:55.773 --> 00:06:57.268
All right, I'll go if you're scared.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:58.551
Scared?

00:06:58.956 --> 00:07:00.068
Flip the damn coin.

00:07:03.767 --> 00:07:04.563
Call it in the air...

00:07:04.826 --> 00:07:05.405
Chicken.

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:08.034
I'm going.

00:07:08.102 --> 00:07:09.011
I said I'd go.

00:07:09.324 --> 00:07:10.333
I'm going.

00:07:10.752 --> 00:07:11.600
All right.

00:07:13.509 --> 00:07:14.858
Don't drop me.

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.107
So, you found some beetles

00:07:21.212 --> 00:07:22.550
In a hole in the ground.

00:07:23.429 --> 00:07:24.860
That's shocking, Sam.

00:07:25.388 --> 00:07:27.429
There were no tunnels, no tracks,

00:07:27.852 --> 00:07:30.385
No evidence of any other
kind of creature down there.

00:07:30.635 --> 00:07:32.386
You know, some beetles do eat meat.

00:07:32.405 --> 00:07:35.192
Now, it's usually dead meat, but...
How many did you find down there?

00:07:35.464 --> 00:07:35.924
10.

00:07:37.365 --> 00:07:39.730
It would take a whole lot more than
that to eat out somebody's brain.

00:07:39.843 --> 00:07:41.063
Well, maybe there were more.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:43.502
I don't know. It sounds
like a stretch to me.

00:07:43.524 --> 00:07:46.362
We need more information on
the area, the neighborhood,

00:07:46.386 --> 00:07:49.025
Whether something like this
has ever happened before.

00:07:51.007 --> 00:07:51.524
What?

00:07:52.239 --> 00:07:53.588
I know a good place to start.

00:07:55.154 --> 00:07:57.429
I'm kind of hungry for a
little barbecue, how about you?

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:01.652
What, we can't talk to the locals?

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:04.874
And the free food's got nothing to do
with it? Of course not. I'm a professional.

00:08:05.456 --> 00:08:05.953
Right.

00:08:25.913 --> 00:08:28.491
Growing up in a place like
this would freak me out.

00:08:29.157 --> 00:08:29.795
Why?

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:34.362
The manicured lawns, the"how
was your day, honey?"...

00:08:34.462 --> 00:08:35.940
I'd blow my brains out.

00:08:37.395 --> 00:08:39.213
There's nothing wrong with normal.

00:08:40.445 --> 00:08:42.380
I'd take our family over normal any day.

00:08:46.598 --> 00:08:48.440
Welcome. Is this the barbecue?

00:08:48.534 --> 00:08:50.774
Yeah, not the best weather, but...

00:08:50.962 --> 00:08:54.704
I'm Larry Pike, the developer here,
and you are? Dean. This is Sam.

00:08:54.968 --> 00:08:56.563
Sam, Dean, good to meet you.

00:08:56.974 --> 00:08:59.578
So, you two are interested
in Oasis Plains? Yes, sir.

00:09:00.106 --> 00:09:00.962
Let me just say

00:09:01.068 --> 00:09:04.552
That we accept homeowners of
any race,religion, color, or...

00:09:05.122 --> 00:09:06.448
Sexual orientation.

00:09:08.078 --> 00:09:09.099
We're brothers.

00:09:09.881 --> 00:09:13.729
Our father is getting on in years, and
we're just looking for a place for him.

00:09:13.823 --> 00:09:14.409
Great,

00:09:14.597 --> 00:09:16.720
Great. Well, seniors are
welcome, too. Come on in.

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:22.889
You said you were the developer?

00:09:23.088 --> 00:09:25.975
18 months ago, I was walking
this valley with my survey team.

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:29.098
There was nothing here but
scrub brush and squirrels,

00:09:29.296 --> 00:09:31.914
And you know what? We built
such a nice place to live

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:34.607
That I actually bought into
it myself. This is our house.

00:09:34.776 --> 00:09:39.012
We're the first family in Oasis
Plains. This is my wife, Joanie.

00:09:39.088 --> 00:09:39.951
Hi, there. Hi,

00:09:39.998 --> 00:09:41.556
Nice to meet you. Sam and Dean.

00:09:41.717 --> 00:09:43.031
Sam. Joannie.

00:09:43.087 --> 00:09:44.814
Tell them how much you
love the place, honey.

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:48.141
And lie if you have to because
I need to sell some houses.

00:09:49.258 --> 00:09:50.694
Boys, if you'll excuse me.

00:09:51.548 --> 00:09:55.104
Don't let his salesman routine scare
you. This really is a great place to live.

00:09:55.246 --> 00:09:57.132
Hi, I'm Linda Bloom, head of sales.

00:09:57.226 --> 00:09:58.868
And Linda was second to move in.

00:09:58.981 --> 00:10:00.764
She's a very noisy neighbor, though.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.835
She's kidding, of course.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.716
I take it you two are interested
in becoming homeowners.

00:10:07.421 --> 00:10:08.650
Well... Y-Yeah.

00:10:08.653 --> 00:10:13.859
Well, let me just say that we accept
homeowners of any race, religion, color,or...

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.252
Sexual orientation.

00:10:16.615 --> 00:10:17.108
Hmm.

00:10:17.272 --> 00:10:17.976
Right.

00:10:18.351 --> 00:10:20.463
Uh, I'm gonna go talk to Larry.

00:10:20.791 --> 00:10:21.659
Okay, honey?

00:10:27.317 --> 00:10:28.877
You have three choices...

00:10:28.995 --> 00:10:31.047
Carpet, hardwood, and tile.

00:10:31.118 --> 00:10:31.845
Whoa,

00:10:32.514 --> 00:10:33.886
Someone likes bugs.

00:10:34.508 --> 00:10:37.523
My son. He's into insects.

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:39.758
He's very inquisitive.

00:10:40.509 --> 00:10:41.130
Hmm.

00:10:41.283 --> 00:10:44.509
Who can say no to a steam
shower? I use mine every day.

00:10:44.919 --> 00:10:45.940
Sounds great.

00:10:46.075 --> 00:10:49.336
You also have three different
whirlpool tubs to choose from.

00:10:49.343 --> 00:10:51.522
The hardware for the tubs
include nickel, brass,

00:10:51.574 --> 00:10:54.557
And when you see the kitchens,
you can choose from... Excuse me.

00:10:54.602 --> 00:10:56.021
Um, okay.

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:09.371
Is this yours?

00:11:09.694 --> 00:11:11.351
You gonna tell my dad? I don't know.

00:11:11.541 --> 00:11:12.483
Who's your dad?

00:11:13.188 --> 00:11:13.873
Yeah.

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:16.610
Larry usually skips me in
the family introductions.

00:11:16.715 --> 00:11:20.281
Ouch. First-Name basis with the
old man... sounds pretty grim.

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:22.252
Well, I'm not exactly brochure material.

00:11:22.572 --> 00:11:24.924
Well, hang in there. It gets
better. Alright? I promise.

00:11:25.458 --> 00:11:26.068
When?

00:11:26.091 --> 00:11:26.713
Matthew!

00:11:35.869 --> 00:11:38.215
I am so sorry about my son and his...

00:11:38.344 --> 00:11:39.834
Pet. It's no bother.

00:11:40.338 --> 00:11:41.394
Excuse us.

00:11:48.612 --> 00:11:49.785
Remind you of somebody?

00:11:54.536 --> 00:11:55.169
Dad?

00:11:56.654 --> 00:11:57.980
Dad never treated us like that.

00:11:58.766 --> 00:12:00.854
Well, dad never treated you
like that. You were perfect.

00:12:00.865 --> 00:12:02.343
He was all over my case.

00:12:04.098 --> 00:12:05.283
You don't remember?

00:12:06.162 --> 00:12:08.555
Maybe he had to raise his voice,
but sometimes you were out of line.

00:12:08.572 --> 00:12:09.294
Right.

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:13.177
Right, like when I said I'd rather
play soccer than learn bow hunting.

00:12:13.371 --> 00:12:14.920
Bow hunting's an important skill.

00:12:16.057 --> 00:12:16.796
Whatever.

00:12:18.181 --> 00:12:19.917
How was your tour?

00:12:20.104 --> 00:12:22.110
It was excellent.I'm ready to buy.

00:12:22.305 --> 00:12:24.112
So you might be onto something.

00:12:24.745 --> 00:12:27.443
Looks like Dustin Burwash wasn't
the first strange death around here.

00:12:27.607 --> 00:12:28.205
What happened?

00:12:28.362 --> 00:12:30.212
About a year ago,
before they broke ground,

00:12:30.272 --> 00:12:32.511
One of Larry's surveyors
dropped dead while on the job.

00:12:32.859 --> 00:12:35.436
Get this... severe allergic
reaction to bee stings.

00:12:35.752 --> 00:12:36.984
More bugs. More bugs.

00:12:39.547 --> 00:12:41.912
I've heard of killer
bees, but killer beetles?

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:43.996
What is it that could
make different bugs attack?

00:12:45.761 --> 00:12:48.683
Well, hauntings sometimes
include bug manifestations.

00:12:48.718 --> 00:12:51.199
Yeah, but I didn't see any
evidence of ghost activity.

00:12:51.349 --> 00:12:52.449
Yeah, me neither.

00:12:54.247 --> 00:12:57.394
Maybe they're being controlled
somehow... by something or someone.

00:12:57.929 --> 00:12:59.172
You mean like "Willard"?

00:12:59.206 --> 00:13:00.792
Yeah, bugs instead of rats.

00:13:02.316 --> 00:13:07.844
There are cases of psychic connections between
people and animals, elementals, telepaths.

00:13:07.856 --> 00:13:09.944
Yeah, that whole Timmy/Lassie thing.

00:13:11.254 --> 00:13:12.532
Larry's kid...

00:13:13.107 --> 00:13:14.362
Bugs for pets.

00:13:14.831 --> 00:13:15.981
Matt? Yeah.

00:13:17.784 --> 00:13:21.186
He did try to scare the realtor with
a tarantula. Think he's our willard?

00:13:21.373 --> 00:13:22.288
I don't know.

00:13:22.347 --> 00:13:23.989
Anything's possible, I guess.

00:13:26.167 --> 00:13:28.055
Ooh, hey, pull over here.

00:13:36.918 --> 00:13:38.314
What are we doing here?

00:13:42.185 --> 00:13:43.768
It's too late to talk to anybody else.

00:13:45.701 --> 00:13:48.117
We're gonna squat in an empty house?

00:13:48.739 --> 00:13:50.693
I want to try the steam shower. Come on.

00:13:51.608 --> 00:13:52.476
Come on!

00:14:20.133 --> 00:14:23.440
Atoko valley county began
mandatory insecticide

00:14:23.478 --> 00:14:26.209
Spraying across a wide
swath of the district today.

00:14:26.249 --> 00:14:31.982
Authorities say the decision to spray was made
because of several recent cases of west nile virus,

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:36.489
Coupled with a dramatic increase in
the mosquito population in some areas.

00:14:36.809 --> 00:14:41.292
Although some residents cite concerns about
the high levels of pesticide being used...

00:15:06.525 --> 00:15:09.763
Aaah! Aaah!

00:15:39.331 --> 00:15:40.570
You ever coming out of there?

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:41.640
What?!

00:15:41.912 --> 00:15:44.887
Dean, a police call came
in on the scanner. Hold on.

00:15:44.929 --> 00:15:47.800
Someone was found dead three
blocks from here. Come on.

00:15:50.364 --> 00:15:51.838
This shower is awesome.

00:15:52.072 --> 00:15:52.948
Come on.

00:16:21.188 --> 00:16:23.328
Okay, look, I don't know
anything more right now.

00:16:23.375 --> 00:16:24.989
I'll have to call you back.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:25.843
All right.

00:16:27.251 --> 00:16:28.978
Hello, you're back early.

00:16:28.996 --> 00:16:32.609
Yeah, we wanted to take another look
at the neighborhood. What's going on?

00:16:34.855 --> 00:16:38.308
You guys met Linda
Bloom at the barbecue?

00:16:38.486 --> 00:16:39.322
The realtor.

00:16:39.903 --> 00:16:40.936
Well, she, uh,

00:16:41.831 --> 00:16:43.041
Passed away last night.

00:16:44.496 --> 00:16:45.190
What happened?

00:16:46.553 --> 00:16:47.839
I'm still trying to find out.

00:16:48.402 --> 00:16:50.204
I identified the body for the police.

00:16:51.733 --> 00:16:53.460
I'm sorry. This isn't a good time.

00:16:53.724 --> 00:16:54.325
It's okay.

00:16:54.484 --> 00:16:55.357
Excuse me.

00:16:58.747 --> 00:17:00.052
You know what we have to do, right?

00:17:01.196 --> 00:17:03.786
We got to get in that house.
See if we got a bug problem.

00:17:31.382 --> 00:17:32.902
This looks like the place.

00:17:46.576 --> 00:17:47.468
Spiders.

00:17:48.189 --> 00:17:49.374
From spider boy?

00:17:49.562 --> 00:17:50.312
Matt.

00:17:52.119 --> 00:17:52.905
Maybe.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.633
Isn't his house that way?

00:18:17.692 --> 00:18:18.642
Yep.

00:18:22.149 --> 00:18:23.663
So where's he going?

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:50.545
Hey, Matt.

00:18:51.355 --> 00:18:52.364
Remember me?

00:18:53.321 --> 00:18:54.294
What are you doing out here?

00:18:54.412 --> 00:18:55.784
We want to talk to you.

00:18:57.368 --> 00:18:58.916
You're not here to buy a house, are you?

00:18:59.956 --> 00:19:00.718
Wait,

00:19:01.539 --> 00:19:02.830
You're not serial killers?

00:19:03.182 --> 00:19:05.281
No, no. No, I think you're safe.

00:19:06.618 --> 00:19:07.651
So, Matt...

00:19:08.798 --> 00:19:10.639
You sure know a lot about insects.

00:19:11.765 --> 00:19:12.340
So?

00:19:13.534 --> 00:19:15.681
Did you hear what happened
to Linda, the realtor?

00:19:17.499 --> 00:19:18.871
I hear she died this morning.

00:19:19.054 --> 00:19:20.133
Mm, that's right.

00:19:20.497 --> 00:19:21.740
Spider bites.

00:19:22.608 --> 00:19:23.359
Matt,

00:19:24.227 --> 00:19:26.526
You tried to scare her with a spider.

00:19:28.153 --> 00:19:28.751
Wait,

00:19:29.443 --> 00:19:30.874
You think I had
something to do with that?

00:19:31.461 --> 00:19:32.528
You tell us.

00:19:33.326 --> 00:19:35.320
That tarantula was a joke.

00:19:35.918 --> 00:19:39.408
Anyway, that wouldn't explain the
bee attack or the gas-Company guy.

00:19:40.768 --> 00:19:42.071
You know about those?

00:19:42.505 --> 00:19:43.877
There is something going on here.

00:19:44.346 --> 00:19:45.437
I don't know what,

00:19:45.539 --> 00:19:46.020
But

00:19:46.443 --> 00:19:48.261
Something's happening with the insects.

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:50.008
Let me show you something.

00:19:57.856 --> 00:20:00.858
So, if you knew about all this
bug stuff, why not tell your dad?

00:20:00.964 --> 00:20:02.794
Maybe he could clear everybody out.

00:20:02.958 --> 00:20:04.671
Believe me, I've tried, but

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:06.701
Larry doesn't listen to me.

00:20:06.947 --> 00:20:07.604
Why not?

00:20:07.956 --> 00:20:08.941
Mostly?

00:20:09.082 --> 00:20:11.065
He's too disappointed in his freak son.

00:20:12.836 --> 00:20:13.751
I hear ya.

00:20:14.428 --> 00:20:15.202
You do?

00:20:17.501 --> 00:20:18.662
Matt, how old are you?

00:20:18.733 --> 00:20:19.530
16.

00:20:20.868 --> 00:20:23.624
Well, don't sweat it 'cause in two
years something great's gonna happen.

00:20:24.304 --> 00:20:25.617
What? College.

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:28.714
You'll be able to get out of
that house and away from your dad.

00:20:29.301 --> 00:20:31.802
What kind of advice is that? A
kid should stick with his family.

00:20:36.928 --> 00:20:37.961
How much further, Matt?

00:20:38.133 --> 00:20:39.141
We're close.

00:21:00.465 --> 00:21:02.671
I've been keeping track of
the insect population. It's

00:21:02.893 --> 00:21:04.653
Part of an A.P. Science class.

00:21:06.002 --> 00:21:07.269
You two are like peas in a pod.

00:21:09.331 --> 00:21:10.257
What's been happening?

00:21:10.492 --> 00:21:11.313
A lot.

00:21:12.005 --> 00:21:14.527
I mean, from bees to earthworms,

00:21:14.957 --> 00:21:16.083
Beetles...

00:21:16.212 --> 00:21:17.690
You name it. It's

00:21:17.748 --> 00:21:19.543
Like they're congregating here.

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:20.259
Why?

00:21:20.775 --> 00:21:21.701
I don't know.

00:21:24.326 --> 00:21:25.112
What's that?

00:22:01.937 --> 00:22:03.122
There's something down there.

00:22:09.808 --> 00:22:11.181
Oh, come on.

00:23:01.632 --> 00:23:04.385
So, a bunch of skeletons
in an unmarked grave.

00:23:04.502 --> 00:23:06.473
Yeah, maybe this is a haunting...

00:23:06.602 --> 00:23:07.904
Some pissed-Off spirits,

00:23:08.244 --> 00:23:10.542
Some unfinished business. Yeah, maybe.

00:23:10.624 --> 00:23:12.583
The question is, why bugs

00:23:12.700 --> 00:23:13.768
And why now?

00:23:14.225 --> 00:23:15.703
That's two questions.

00:23:17.029 --> 00:23:18.648
So, with that kid back there...

00:23:18.984 --> 00:23:21.471
How could you tell him to just
ditch his family like that?

00:23:21.682 --> 00:23:22.879
Just, uh,

00:23:23.278 --> 00:23:24.943
I know what the kid's going through.

00:23:25.267 --> 00:23:28.751
How about telling him to respect his old
man? How's that for advice? Dean, come on.

00:23:29.455 --> 00:23:31.132
This isn't about his old man.

00:23:31.214 --> 00:23:32.517
You think I didn't respect dad.

00:23:32.634 --> 00:23:33.854
That's what this is about.

00:23:34.998 --> 00:23:36.464
Just forget it. Sorry I brought it up.

00:23:36.523 --> 00:23:37.555
I respected him,

00:23:38.318 --> 00:23:39.702
But no matter what I did,

00:23:39.948 --> 00:23:41.192
It was never good enough.

00:23:41.309 --> 00:23:43.972
What are you saying, that dad
was disappointed in you? Was?

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:46.153
Is...

00:23:46.623 --> 00:23:48.757
Always has been. Why
would you think that?

00:23:48.804 --> 00:23:50.540
Because I didn't want to bow hunt

00:23:50.709 --> 00:23:53.653
Or hustle pool, because I wanted
to go to school and live my life,

00:23:53.668 --> 00:23:56.052
Which in our whacked-Out
family made me the freak.

00:23:58.127 --> 00:24:00.461
Yeah, you were kind of like the
blond chick in "the munsters."

00:24:01.799 --> 00:24:02.444
Dean,

00:24:03.183 --> 00:24:05.728
You know what most dads are when
their kids score a full ride?

00:24:06.702 --> 00:24:07.417
Proud.

00:24:08.919 --> 00:24:11.112
Most dads don't toss their
kids out of the house.

00:24:12.457 --> 00:24:13.712
I remember that fight.

00:24:14.779 --> 00:24:17.536
In fact, I seem to recall a few choice
phrases coming out of your mouth.

00:24:22.339 --> 00:24:23.114
You know,

00:24:23.630 --> 00:24:26.316
Truth is, when we finally do find dad,

00:24:27.243 --> 00:24:29.272
I don't know if he's
even gonna want to see me.

00:24:31.055 --> 00:24:33.056
Sam, dad was never disappointed in you.

00:24:34.288 --> 00:24:34.980
Never.

00:24:36.247 --> 00:24:37.432
He was scared.

00:24:38.155 --> 00:24:39.328
What are you talking about?

00:24:39.375 --> 00:24:42.038
He was afraid of what could have
happened to you if he wasn't around.

00:24:43.563 --> 00:24:45.263
But even when you two weren't talking,

00:24:46.104 --> 00:24:48.345
He used to swing by
Stanford whenever he could,

00:24:49.107 --> 00:24:50.057
Keep an eye on you,

00:24:50.796 --> 00:24:52.087
Make sure you were safe.

00:24:52.779 --> 00:24:53.717
What?

00:24:55.133 --> 00:24:55.778
Yeah.

00:24:59.943 --> 00:25:01.585
Why didn't he tell me any of that?

00:25:03.549 --> 00:25:06.118
It's a two-Way street, dude. You
could have picked up the phone.

00:25:11.901 --> 00:25:13.736
Come on, we're gonna be
late for our appointment.

00:25:22.053 --> 00:25:23.566
So, you two are students?

00:25:23.991 --> 00:25:25.058
Yeah.

00:25:25.164 --> 00:25:27.416
Yeah, we're in your class.

00:25:27.663 --> 00:25:28.965
Anthro 101.

00:25:29.363 --> 00:25:30.525
Oh, yeah.

00:25:30.595 --> 00:25:31.369
So,

00:25:31.440 --> 00:25:33.410
What about the bones, Professor?

00:25:34.288 --> 00:25:37.045
This is quite an
interesting find you've made.

00:25:37.092 --> 00:25:41.139
I'd say they're 170
years old, give or take.

00:25:41.725 --> 00:25:43.555
The time frame and the geography

00:25:43.574 --> 00:25:45.498
Heavily suggest native american.

00:25:45.944 --> 00:25:49.281
Were there any tribes or
reservations on that land?

00:25:49.363 --> 00:25:52.061
Not according to the historical record,

00:25:52.132 --> 00:25:53.059
But

00:25:53.493 --> 00:25:54.701
The, uh...

00:25:54.748 --> 00:25:58.889
Relocation of native peoples
was quite common at that time.

00:25:59.135 --> 00:25:59.874
Right.

00:26:00.678 --> 00:26:01.312
Well,

00:26:01.828 --> 00:26:03.364
Are there any local legends,

00:26:03.576 --> 00:26:05.793
Oral histories about the area?

00:26:06.778 --> 00:26:07.963
Well...

00:26:08.573 --> 00:26:12.139
You know, there's a
euchee tribe in Sapulpa.

00:26:12.369 --> 00:26:14.128
It's about 60 miles from here.

00:26:15.536 --> 00:26:17.503
Someone out there might know the truth.

00:26:20.612 --> 00:26:21.644
All right.

00:27:08.038 --> 00:27:09.242
Joe Whitetree?

00:27:10.968 --> 00:27:13.983
We'd like to ask you a few
questions, if that's all right.

00:27:14.587 --> 00:27:16.124
We're students from the university.

00:27:16.182 --> 00:27:18.235
No, you're not. You're lying.

00:27:20.276 --> 00:27:21.074
Um,

00:27:21.672 --> 00:27:24.464
The truth is... You know
who starts sentence with

00:27:24.589 --> 00:27:25.669
"Truth is"?

00:27:26.067 --> 00:27:27.064
Liars.

00:27:31.963 --> 00:27:33.722
Have you heard of Oasis Plains?

00:27:33.769 --> 00:27:36.232
It's a housing development
near the Atoka valley.

00:27:38.948 --> 00:27:39.969
I like him.

00:27:40.661 --> 00:27:41.893
He's not a liar.

00:27:42.984 --> 00:27:44.157
I know the area.

00:27:45.541 --> 00:27:47.535
What can you tell us
about the history there?

00:27:47.672 --> 00:27:48.775
Why do you want to know?

00:27:49.444 --> 00:27:50.687
Something...

00:27:51.086 --> 00:27:52.153
Something bad

00:27:53.021 --> 00:27:54.992
Is happening in Oasis Plains.

00:27:55.959 --> 00:27:59.654
We think it might have something to do
with some old bones we found down there...

00:28:00.863 --> 00:28:02.329
Native american bones.

00:28:07.192 --> 00:28:09.503
I'll tell you what my
grandfather told me,

00:28:10.265 --> 00:28:12.107
What his grandfather told him.

00:28:12.857 --> 00:28:14.335
200 years ago,

00:28:14.602 --> 00:28:17.335
A band of my ancestors
lived in that valley.

00:28:18.086 --> 00:28:21.687
One day, the american
calvary came to relocate them.

00:28:24.770 --> 00:28:26.365
They were resistant...

00:28:26.999 --> 00:28:28.665
Calvary impatient.

00:28:30.248 --> 00:28:32.019
As my grandfather put it,

00:28:33.052 --> 00:28:33.887
On a night,

00:28:34.016 --> 00:28:35.060
The moon

00:28:35.388 --> 00:28:36.350
And the sun

00:28:36.631 --> 00:28:38.872
Shared the sky as equals,

00:28:40.162 --> 00:28:42.848
The calvary first raided our village.

00:28:43.466 --> 00:28:44.499
They murdered,

00:28:45.202 --> 00:28:46.035
Raped.

00:28:47.114 --> 00:28:49.470
The next day, the calvary came again,

00:28:49.752 --> 00:28:51.851
And the next and the next.

00:28:52.250 --> 00:28:55.347
And on the sixth night, the
calvary came one last time,

00:28:56.492 --> 00:28:58.510
And by the time the sun rose,

00:28:58.686 --> 00:29:00.820
Every man, woman, and child

00:29:00.891 --> 00:29:02.624
Still in the village

00:29:02.976 --> 00:29:04.008
Was dead.

00:29:08.625 --> 00:29:10.455
They say on the sixth night,

00:29:10.608 --> 00:29:13.212
As the chief of the village lay dying,

00:29:13.564 --> 00:29:15.440
He whispered to the heavens

00:29:16.285 --> 00:29:19.616
That no white man would
ever tarnish this land again.

00:29:20.536 --> 00:29:21.545
Nature

00:29:21.920 --> 00:29:23.105
Would rise up

00:29:23.773 --> 00:29:25.357
And protect the valley,

00:29:25.521 --> 00:29:28.606
And it would bring as many
days of misery and death

00:29:29.177 --> 00:29:30.326
To the white man

00:29:30.983 --> 00:29:33.106
As the calvary had
brought upon his people.

00:29:34.901 --> 00:29:35.992
Insects.

00:29:36.880 --> 00:29:38.299
That sounds like nature to me.

00:29:39.848 --> 00:29:40.915
Six days?

00:29:41.185 --> 00:29:43.285
And on the night of the sixth day,

00:29:44.183 --> 00:29:45.814
None would survive.

00:29:54.243 --> 00:29:56.155
When did the gas-Company man die?

00:29:57.140 --> 00:29:59.744
Let's see, we got here
tuesday, so friday the 20th.

00:30:00.265 --> 00:30:01.168
March 20th.

00:30:02.118 --> 00:30:03.549
That's the spring equinox.

00:30:04.253 --> 00:30:06.611
The night, the sun and the
moon share the sky as equals.

00:30:06.707 --> 00:30:10.542
So every year about this time,
anybody in Oasis Plains is in danger.

00:30:11.211 --> 00:30:14.796
Larry built his neighborhood on cursed land.
And on the sixth night... that's tonight.

00:30:15.125 --> 00:30:18.550
If we don't do something, Larry's
family will be dead by sunrise.

00:30:19.895 --> 00:30:21.303
So how do we break a curse?

00:30:21.631 --> 00:30:22.769
You don't break a curse.

00:30:23.168 --> 00:30:25.350
You get out of its way. We got
to get those people out now.

00:31:43.564 --> 00:31:46.579
Yes, mr. Pike, there's a main-Line
gas leak in your neighborhood.

00:31:46.661 --> 00:31:48.209
God, really? And how big?

00:31:48.315 --> 00:31:51.060
Well, it's fairly extensive.
I don't want to alarm you, but

00:31:51.189 --> 00:31:55.001
We need your family out of the vicinity for
at least 12 hours or so, just to be safe.

00:31:55.139 --> 00:31:56.148
And who is this again?

00:31:56.207 --> 00:31:58.940
Travis Weaver. I work for
Oklahoma gas and power.

00:31:58.987 --> 00:31:59.561
Uh-Huh.

00:31:59.770 --> 00:32:03.606
The problemis I know Travis. He's worked
with us for a year. So who is this?

00:32:04.134 --> 00:32:05.152
Uh...

00:32:06.842 --> 00:32:07.886
Give me the phone.

00:32:16.876 --> 00:32:17.509
Hello?

00:32:17.626 --> 00:32:18.623
Matt, it's Sam.

00:32:18.905 --> 00:32:20.907
Sam, my backyard's
crawling with cockroaches.

00:32:20.908 --> 00:32:24.356
Matt, just listen. You have to get your
family out of that house right now, okay?

00:32:24.648 --> 00:32:25.502
What, why?

00:32:26.390 --> 00:32:27.639
Because something's coming.

00:32:28.296 --> 00:32:29.132
More bugs.

00:32:29.480 --> 00:32:30.738
Yeah, a lot more.

00:32:31.828 --> 00:32:33.922
My dad doesn't listen in
the best of circumstances.

00:32:33.942 --> 00:32:36.889
What am I supposed to tell him?
You got to make him listen, okay?

00:32:37.088 --> 00:32:38.321
Give me the phone. Give me the phone!

00:32:38.532 --> 00:32:41.679
Matt, under no circumstances are you to
tell the truth. He'll just think you're nuts.

00:32:41.808 --> 00:32:44.332
But he's my... Tell him you have
a sharp pain in your right side,

00:32:44.391 --> 00:32:45.952
And you got to go to the hospital, okay?

00:32:46.083 --> 00:32:47.774
Yeah. Yeah, okay.

00:32:51.625 --> 00:32:52.658
"Make him listen."

00:32:53.362 --> 00:32:54.454
What are you thinking?

00:33:06.495 --> 00:33:08.126
Damn it, they're still here. Come on.

00:33:15.957 --> 00:33:18.137
Get off my property
before I call the cops!

00:33:18.184 --> 00:33:19.863
Mr. Pike, listen. Dad,

00:33:20.368 --> 00:33:21.389
They're just trying to help.

00:33:21.436 --> 00:33:22.493
Get in the house!

00:33:23.044 --> 00:33:24.712
Sorry. I told him the truth.

00:33:24.770 --> 00:33:26.602
We had a plan, Matt.
What happened to the plan?

00:33:27.412 --> 00:33:29.020
Look, it's twelve a.M.

00:33:29.161 --> 00:33:30.558
They are coming any minute now.

00:33:30.617 --> 00:33:33.704
You need to get your family
and go before it's too late.

00:33:33.835 --> 00:33:35.830
Oh, yeah, you mean
before the biblical swarm.

00:33:36.006 --> 00:33:38.437
What do you think really
happened to that realtor, huh?

00:33:38.578 --> 00:33:39.975
And the gas-Company guy?

00:33:40.421 --> 00:33:42.240
You don't think something
weird's going on around here?

00:33:42.360 --> 00:33:44.673
Look, I don't know who
you are, but you're crazy.

00:33:44.686 --> 00:33:47.146
You come near my boy or my family again,

00:33:47.243 --> 00:33:48.318
We're gonna have a problem.

00:33:48.363 --> 00:33:51.037
Well, I hate to be a downer, but we got
a problem right now. Dad, they're right.

00:33:51.256 --> 00:33:52.188
We're in danger.

00:33:53.150 --> 00:33:55.163
Matt, get inside now!

00:33:55.539 --> 00:33:56.583
Why won't you listen to me?!

00:33:56.673 --> 00:33:59.043
Because this is crazy!
It doesn't make any sense!

00:33:59.366 --> 00:33:59.900
Look,

00:34:00.160 --> 00:34:01.768
This land is cursed.

00:34:02.106 --> 00:34:05.510
People have died here. Are you gonna
really take that risk with your family?

00:34:05.522 --> 00:34:06.033
Wait.

00:34:08.212 --> 00:34:08.926
You hear it?

00:34:13.346 --> 00:34:14.405
What the hell?

00:34:19.011 --> 00:34:21.077
It's time to go. Larry, get your wife.

00:34:21.798 --> 00:34:22.219
Guys.

00:34:26.447 --> 00:34:27.536
Oh, my god.

00:34:29.616 --> 00:34:30.826
We'll never make it.

00:34:30.878 --> 00:34:32.854
Everybody in the house.
Everybody in the house!

00:34:33.070 --> 00:34:33.739
Let's go!

00:34:38.678 --> 00:34:40.858
Is there anyone else in the
neighborhood? No, it's just us.

00:34:41.497 --> 00:34:42.699
Honey, what's happening?

00:34:43.259 --> 00:34:44.303
What's that noise?

00:34:45.468 --> 00:34:46.437
Call 911.

00:34:47.256 --> 00:34:48.133
Joanie!

00:34:48.389 --> 00:34:49.020
Okay.

00:34:50.275 --> 00:34:51.870
I need towels.

00:34:51.982 --> 00:34:55.242
We got to lock this place up. Come on, doors,
windows, the fireplace, everything. Okay?

00:34:55.941 --> 00:34:56.954
Phones are dead.

00:34:57.035 --> 00:34:58.393
They must have chewed
through the phone lines.

00:35:04.563 --> 00:35:05.597
And the power lines.

00:35:05.838 --> 00:35:06.691
Maybe my cell.

00:35:10.004 --> 00:35:10.946
No signal.

00:35:11.513 --> 00:35:12.487
You won't get one.

00:35:13.220 --> 00:35:14.880
They're blanketing the house.

00:35:31.897 --> 00:35:32.955
So, what do we do now?

00:35:33.682 --> 00:35:34.673
We try to outlast it.

00:35:36.711 --> 00:35:39.469
Hopefully the curse will
end at sunrise. Hopefully?

00:36:02.485 --> 00:36:04.270
Bug spray? Trust me.

00:36:07.229 --> 00:36:07.776
What is that?

00:36:18.281 --> 00:36:19.161
The flue.

00:36:21.975 --> 00:36:23.748
I think everybody needs to get upstairs.

00:36:34.968 --> 00:36:37.226
Everybody upstairs now! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:36:40.607 --> 00:36:41.956
Quick!

00:36:50.763 --> 00:36:53.248
Okay, Joanie, go, go, go.

00:36:53.285 --> 00:36:54.236
Matt, go.

00:36:55.797 --> 00:36:56.888
Hurry!

00:37:03.666 --> 00:37:04.652
You in? Yeah.

00:37:07.812 --> 00:37:09.574
Come on!

00:37:16.185 --> 00:37:17.582
My god, what's that?!

00:37:23.915 --> 00:37:25.161
Something's eating through the wood.

00:37:26.587 --> 00:37:27.428
Termites.

00:37:31.870 --> 00:37:33.259
All right, everybody get back.

00:37:33.414 --> 00:37:34.856
Get back! Get back!

00:37:34.886 --> 00:37:35.456
Get back!

00:37:36.530 --> 00:37:37.318
Matt.

00:38:39.099 --> 00:38:41.492
Huddle together. Cover your faces.

00:38:52.252 --> 00:38:53.015
Look!

00:39:54.382 --> 00:39:55.328
What, no goodbye?

00:39:55.853 --> 00:39:56.694
Good timing.

00:39:56.807 --> 00:39:58.278
Another hour and we'd have been gone.

00:39:58.834 --> 00:39:59.449
For good?

00:40:00.388 --> 00:40:00.998
Yeah.

00:40:01.051 --> 00:40:04.820
The development's been put on hold while the
government investigates those bones you found,

00:40:05.255 --> 00:40:06.644
But I'm gonna make damn sure

00:40:06.774 --> 00:40:07.908
No one lives here again.

00:40:08.704 --> 00:40:10.152
You don't seem too upset about it.

00:40:11.385 --> 00:40:14.621
Well, this has been the biggest
financial disaster of my career, but,

00:40:16.047 --> 00:40:17.158
Somehow...

00:40:19.059 --> 00:40:20.366
I really don't care.

00:40:35.651 --> 00:40:36.560
What's this?

00:40:36.792 --> 00:40:37.618
I don't know.

00:40:38.827 --> 00:40:39.510
They

00:40:39.788 --> 00:40:41.109
Kind of weird me out now.

00:40:43.690 --> 00:40:45.090
Yeah, I should hope so.

00:41:06.116 --> 00:41:07.197
I want to find dad.

00:41:09.004 --> 00:41:09.807
Yeah, me too.

00:41:11.421 --> 00:41:12.525
Yeah, but I just...

00:41:15.915 --> 00:41:17.341
I want to apologize to him.

00:41:20.884 --> 00:41:21.508
For what?

00:41:24.082 --> 00:41:25.793
All the things I said to him.

00:41:28.651 --> 00:41:30.115
He was just doing the best he could.

00:41:33.483 --> 00:41:35.090
Well, don't worry, we'll find him,

00:41:36.298 --> 00:41:37.752
And you'll apologize,

00:41:38.573 --> 00:41:41.196
And within five minutes, you guys
will beat each other's throats.

00:41:45.274 --> 00:41:47.116
Yeah, probably.

00:41:49.872 --> 00:41:51.444
Let's hit the road. Let's.



